1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:05,144
The air conditioning was broken. Twelve people sweated anyway.

2
00:00:04,924 --> 00:00:08,768
"Seventy-two hours," the American side said.

3
00:00:08,548 --> 00:00:11,321
"Fordow is not on this agenda."

4
00:00:11,101 --> 00:00:18,889
Wars begin with gunfire, but their real weight is often decided in rooms where no one says anything at all.

5
00:00:19,089 --> 00:00:23,063
Dr. Leila Shirazi checked the signal three times.

6
00:00:22,843 --> 00:00:28,803
The assessment read "fully neutralized." But the signal held a regular rhythm.

7
00:00:28,583 --> 00:00:31,486
A truly dead system couldn't do that.

8
00:00:31,266 --> 00:00:38,819
The last transmission from a source codenamed ZARRIN: "This is the last transmission."

9
00:00:39,019 --> 00:00:45,371
Washington's 72-hour proposal arrived as a notification, not a consultation.

10
00:00:45,151 --> 00:00:48,811
Israel had been left out of the Islamabad channel.

11
00:00:48,591 --> 00:00:51,077
The world read it as a warning.

12
00:00:50,857 --> 00:00:55,902
It wasn't a warning. It was the announcement of a decision already made.

13
00:00:56,102 --> 00:01:02,271
A throat carrying a fifth of the world's oil opened again after six days.

14
00:01:02,051 --> 00:01:06,991
"The strait's open." "Limited. Northern lane only."

15
00:01:06,771 --> 00:01:10,798
On the horizon, the silhouette of a tanker appeared.

16
00:01:10,578 --> 00:01:15,623
As long as Fordow's signal was alive, the war was not over.

17
00:01:15,823 --> 00:01:22,122
Nine times Captain Kim Junho tried to call. Nine times he stopped.

18
00:01:21,902 --> 00:01:26,347
His mother picked up on the second ring. She'd been waiting.

19
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:29,396
"Junho." Two syllables were enough.

20
00:01:29,176 --> 00:01:35,475
"I'm alive." "I know. Sleep well." She asked nothing else.

21
00:01:35,675 --> 00:01:39,780
Soraya Tahir stood in the middle of Azadi Square and sang.

22
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:44,135
An old Persian song for the end of winter, for flowers opening.

23
00:01:43,915 --> 00:01:48,673
One Basij member set his baton down on the pavement and sang along.

24
00:01:48,453 --> 00:01:52,192
Spring didn't stop. Spring is older than the war.

25
00:01:52,392 --> 00:01:59,580
Professor Azad Moradi opened the last blank page of a notebook he'd bought in 1973.

26
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:04,274
"Freedom is uncomfortable too. But repression hurts longer."

27
00:02:04,054 --> 00:02:07,506
From the courtyard, the singing rose again.

28
00:02:07,706 --> 00:02:11,994
Fordow's signal changed again. Its strength was rising.

29
00:02:11,774 --> 00:02:17,655
"Kinetic intervention alone is not sufficient. The next step is diplomatic."

30
00:02:17,435 --> 00:02:22,115
Bombs bring down buildings, but a signal doesn't stop for a bomb.

31
00:02:21,895 --> 00:02:24,093
Continued in Episode 4.

